Fraud-Detection Model Quality Gates & Live Monitoring
This repository enforces automated data and model quality gates for the xFusionCorp Industries fraud-detection pipeline across two stages:

Pre-Deployment CI Gate (Evidently AI): Validates batch data integrity and classification accuracy before model promotion and publishes snapshots to the Evidently UI workspace.

Post-Deployment Live Alerting (Grafana + Prometheus): Continuously monitors smoothed live prediction accuracy and alerts on-call engineers if performance degrades.

Architecture & Thresholds
Stage	Tooling	Metric / Signal	Gate Condition	Failure Action
CI Batch Gate	Evidently AI (Report(include_tests=True))	DatasetMissingValueCount	< 10 missing values	Fails CI job (FAIL)
CI Batch Gate	Evidently AI (Report(include_tests=True))	Accuracy	> 0.80	Fails CI job (FAIL)
Live Production	Prometheus + Grafana Alerting	avg_over_time(prediction_accuracy[1m])	< 0.80	Fires alert (Low Prediction Accuracy)
Implementation Details
1. Evidently Test Suite (/root/code/monitoring/tests/test_suite.py)
The test suite evaluates /root/code/monitoring/tests/current.csv against a binary classification schema (target="is_fraud", prediction_labels="prediction"), writes structured results to test_results.json, and publishes a run snapshot to the fraud-detector quality gates workspace.

Python
METRICS = [
    DatasetMissingValueCount(tests=[lt(10)]),
    Accuracy(tests=[gt(0.80)]),
]
Run the suite:

Bash
python3 /root/code/monitoring/tests/test_suite.py
2. Grafana Alert Rule (Low Prediction Accuracy)
Provisioned under folder ML Monitoring (ml-monitoring) and rule group fraud-detector-alerts:

Query (A): avg_over_time(prediction_accuracy[1m]) (Prometheus datasource)

Reduce (B): Last value of A

Threshold (C): B < 0.80 (lt evaluator)

